      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "This question involves finding the greatest common factor (GCF) of two numbers, 40 and 48. To find the GCF, we can use the factorization method and the prime factorization method.\nStep 1: Factorization method\nThe prime factors of 40 are 2^3 * 5 and the prime factors of 48 are 2^4 * 3.\nThe GCF is the product of the common prime factors raised to their lowest power. Therefore, the GCF of 40 and 48 is 2^3 = 8.\nGCF of 40 and 48 is 8.",
